packages/blk-wmt: the loader and launcher sequence follows mtk-wmt-init.c from
https://github.com/snowopsdev/omarchy-iplay50-mini-pro (b7fa1570, GPL-2.0). Ioctl numbers and the patch info layouts
follow MediaTek's WMT driver (wmt_detect.h, wmt_dev.c, wmt_lib.h, GPL-2.0) as published in
https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-common (android-15-release-vvob35,
2993f4be). The NVRAM and Wi-Fi power on writes follow MediaTek's wmt_cdev_wifi.c (GPL-2.0, Dual BSD/GPL module) as
published in https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-wlan-adaptor
(android-15-release-vvob35, 11353556).
packages/blk-bt: written from MediaTek's stp_chrdev_bt.c (Dual BSD/GPL) as published in
https://github.com/MotorolaMobilityLLC/vendor-mediatek-kernel_modules-connectivity-bt-mt66xx (2a851b31), the Linux
hci_ldisc and hci_h4 drivers and the Bluetooth Core specification. The firmware quirks it handles (the Read
Synchronization Train Parameters reply, the LE command bits in Read Local Supported Commands, the BD address write
after HCI Reset) were found by https://github.com/snowopsdev/omarchy-iplay50-mini-pro (b7fa1570),
https://github.com/Barley-Project/tb330fu-ubuntu (684d207f) and https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5 (2fa63874).
